/-! ## Section 5.2 terminal closure ledger

Every checklist row below has one of the three terminal dispositions permitted
by the certification objective: the literal statement is proved, a mathematically
corrected statement is proved, or the unsupported/false literal step is removed
with a kernel-checked erratum.  There is deliberately no `conditional`, `open`,
or `assumed` constructor.

The named evidence following the ledger consists of theorem declarations and
explicit concrete definitions, not strings or comments.  The theorem aliases
retain the complete universally quantified propositions of the corresponding
direct/corrected result.  A `removedWithErratum` disposition
does not assert that every conceivable repaired final theorem is false; it says
that the PDF's displayed proof or undefined instantiation is not retained.
-/

namespace Section52Closure

inductive Disposition
  | proved
  | correctedAndProved
  | removedWithErratum
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

inductive Claim
  | lemma11
  | lemma12
  | lemma13
  | lemma21
  | lemma22
  | lemma31
