/-! ### Proof-producing evidence for every terminal Proposition row

Unlike the disposition table, this family contains no `True` fallback.  Each
row is tied to one already proved mathematical statement: a complete universal
corrected theorem, an explicit positive model, or the decisive formal erratum.
The concrete spectral witnesses below establish nonvacuity of the corrected
interfaces without pretending to be the PDF's unspecified Mock-I package. -/

