/-! ### Proof-producing evidence for all four Section 5.4 rows

The disposition table above is only a finite bookkeeping device.  The
following evidence family is deliberately stronger: the first two rows carry
an explicitly constructed positive continuous-spectrum model; Corollary 3.3
carries both its universally quantified repaired theorem and the closed
positive-discrete-mode verification identity above; and Theorem 5.1 stores its
complete universally quantified repaired theorem.  No row is reduced to
`True`.

The concrete model for the first two rows uses the constant nonnegative test,
Dirac spectral measure at zero at every cusp, and unit coefficients.  The
Corollary 3.3 witness instead uses the smooth Fourier-positive test and Lebesgue
spectral measure constructed earlier.  Neither is asserted to be the paper's
unspecified Mock-I spectral package; they are closed nonvacuity witnesses for
the corrected analytic interfaces. -/

open CorrectedLemmas.CorrectedPropositions

/-- A closed continuous-spectral model used to witness Corollaries 3.1 and
3.2.  Its test and coefficients are identically one and every cusp measure is
the Dirac mass at zero. -/
noncomputable def corollary32ConcreteSpectralData : ContinuousSpectralData where
  test := fun _ => 1
  test_nonneg := by
    intro t
    norm_num
  spectralMeasure := fun _ => Measure.dirac 0
  coefficient := fun _ _ _ => 1
  integrable := by
    intro κ m
    exact integrable_dirac (by norm_num)

/-- A concrete fixed-window uniform-activity certificate for the preceding
spectral data.  The window is all of `ℝ`, both positive floors are one, and the
activity sum has one unit contribution from each of the three cusps. -/
noncomputable def corollary32ConcreteUniformActivity :
    CorrectedLemmas.UniformActivity.Data corollary32ConcreteSpectralData where
  window := fun _ => Set.univ
  window_measurable := by
    intro κ
    exact MeasurableSet.univ
  testFloor := 1
  testFloor_pos := by norm_num
  test_lower := by
    intro κ t ht
    norm_num [corollary32ConcreteSpectralData]
  coefficient_integrableOn := by
    intro κ m
    exact (integrable_dirac (by norm_num)).integrableOn
  activityFloor := 1
  activityFloor_pos := by norm_num
  threshold := 1
  threshold_pos := by norm_num
  lowerActivity := by
    intro m hm
    norm_num [corollary32ConcreteSpectralData]

